  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 229 AM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nBy Monday morning, the cold front will have moved through much of\nthe area bringing a more seasonable airmass, although southern\nareas may still be quite warm Monday depending on the specific\ntiming of the front. And the weather through the week will be\ndominated by the post-frontal surface ridge across the Midwest\ninto the Plains. Precipitation chances Monday will primary be\nclosest to the cold front in the south. Later in the week the\nhighest precipitation chances will primarily be across the west\nwith post-frontal upslope surface winds helping to produce\nconvection over the High Plains with the storms moving toward\nwestern portions of the forecast area. Temperatures will remain\ncloser to seasonable averages than we have seen in quite a while.",
